<title>NEW ZEALAND: CRICKET-NEW ZEALAND OUT FOR 153 V ENGLAND IN ONE-DAYER.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-NEW ZEALAND OUT FOR 153 V ENGLAND IN ONE-DAYER.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand, batting first, were all out for 153 in 39.5 overs against England in their fourth one-day cricket international at Eden Park on Sunday.</p>
<p>The match was shortened after rain delayed the start. England have 43 overs to reach their target of 154.</p>
<p>Score: New Zealand 153 (N. Astle 51, R. Croft 2-26).</p>
</text>
